---
// How it works — Mel's three concrete actions to question 3:
//   1. paste a URL
//   2. tag it
//   3. confirm/update the AI's assessment + publish to subscribers
// Mock UI element on the third step gives the page a concrete artifact moment
// without inventing product screenshots.
---

<section id="how-it-works">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">02 · How it works</p>
      <h2>Three actions from link to library.</h2>
    </header>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div class="step__body">
          <h3>Paste a URL</h3>
          <p>Drop any link into the inbox. The system fetches, parses, and prepares a draft entry.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step__demo" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="field field--demo">
            <input type="url" value="https://example.com/prompt-caching-explained" readonly />
            <button type="button">Ingest</button>
          </span>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div class="step__body">
          <h3>Tag it</h3>
          <p>Pick a topic and a depth: <code class="chip">llm-cache</code> <code class="chip">production</code> <code class="chip">verified</code>. Tags become the index your agents will query.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step__demo" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="chip">llm&#8209;cache</span>
          <span class="chip">production</span>
          <span class="chip">verified</span>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div class="step__body">
          <h3>Confirm the AI assessment · publish</h3>
          <p>The system drafts a one&#8209;paragraph verdict and a usefulness score. You skim the source, refine if needed, then publish to subscribers.</p>
        </div>

        <figure class="step__demo card" aria-hidden="true">
          <figcaption>
            <span class="kicker">AI verdict · draft</span>
            <span class="verdict verdict--yes">Useful · 0.78</span>
          </figcaption>
          <p>
            Concrete walk&#8209;through of anthropic.claude&#8209;3 prompt caching with
            measured latency wins and the boundary conditions where it fails.
          </p>
          <ul class="access">
            <li>you · 0 reads</li>
            <li>subscribers · pending publish</li>
          </ul>
        </figure>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--gap-4);
  }

  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    column-gap: var(--gap-3);
    row-gap: var(--gap-2);
    padding-block: var(--gap-3);
    border-top: var(--rule-hair);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .step:first-child { border-top: 0; }

  .step__num {
    grid-row: 1 / span 2;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--ember);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    padding-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  .step__body { grid-column: 2; }
  .step__body p { max-width: 56ch; }

  .step__demo {
    grid-column: 2;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .field--demo { max-width: 28rem; }

  .card {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    max-width: 32rem;
  }

  .card figcaption {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .verdict {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-mono);
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.18rem 0.6rem;
  }
  .verdict--yes { color: var(--verdict-yes); }

  .access {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-mono);
    color: var(--ink-mute);
  }
</style>
